    "model_target": "euromod://FR/bch00_fr/def_const/$bch00_child2_thres2",
    "spine_order": "29",
    "value_type": "scalar",
    "unit": "currency",
    "threshold_unit": null,
    "label": {
      "en": "Income threshold to receive half rate for families with 2 children"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$bch00_child2_thres2"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "This constant is the upper annual household resource (Revenu Net Catégoriel) ceiling for a two-child family to still receive the AF universal child benefit at the reduced (50%) rate, set at €104,719 for 2025 per Table 2.5 of the country report; above this threshold the family receives only the 25% rate. It is used in bch00_fr/BenCalc as the Comp_Cond condition determining the total benefit amount for the two-child means test. It forms the second income band boundary (alongside $bch00_child2_thres1) of the AF income test introduced in July 2015."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Constants"
    },
